						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 1: SCALING TO SIZE\n\nIn this example we have a circle of dots generated by sending a Circle node into a Transform node and applying the Circle pattern to the translation inlet.\nThe Points slider adjusts how much points the circle pattern has.\nWhen we change this the instance count of the Transform node changes accordingly.\n\nBut we are also changing the scale of the dots as the circle closes in on itself using a Linear node.\nWhen we change the amount of points of the Circle Pattern node, we need to update the size of the linear node as well.\nIf we don't do this the scaling pattern will repeat itself.\n\nTry playing with the Points slider and removing the Size node to see the difference."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 631.75421142578125,
					"width": 1814.186767578125,
					"x": 323.20880126953125,
					"y": 248.11651611328125
